# Slightly Parallel — environment configuration
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored); run.sh sources it before launching.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data root — where Slightly Parallel reads and writes agent data
# (scans.csv, snapshots/, projects/, the mutual entity CSVs).
# Default (unset): ~/.slightly-parallel, filled with the shipped demo data on the first start.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SP_DATA_ROOT="/path/to/your/agents-folder"

# Older names (still honored, lower precedence):
# SCAN_DATA_ROOT="/path/to/your/agents-folder"
# DATA_ROOT="/path/to/your/agents-folder"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bind host / port (defaults: 127.0.0.1:8123).
# SP_PORT takes precedence over the older SCAN_PORT and PORT.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# SP_PORT=8123
# Slightly Parallel has no login. A HOST other than 127.0.0.1 opens it to the network,
# and the server starts that way only with this set:
# SP_ALLOW_LAN=1

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CORS allowlist (comma-separated origins).
# Default: localhost/127.0.0.1 on ports 5173 (Vite dev) and 8123.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SP_CORS_ORIGINS="http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:8123"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The terminal is a switch in Settings › Terminal (or the drawer, `),
# off until turned on; nothing is needed here. The server makes its
# own token and hands it only to Slightly Parallel's pages. These two are for
# a scripted setup: the first forces the terminal on, the second
# fixes the token instead of a new one at every start.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SP_ENABLE_TERMINAL=1
# SP_TOKEN="a-long-random-string"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backups. Rotating .tar.gz archives of the whole data root, taken
# on a schedule (see Settings → Backups) and rotated to one per
# rung: a day, 3 days, a week, 2 weeks, a month, 3 months.
# Default (unset): a SIBLING of the data root, "<data_root>-backups".
# It must never sit inside the data root — the server refuses that,
# because an archive there would be swept into the next one and
# deleted by exactly the accident it exists for. Point this at
# another disk or a mounted share and the backups leave the machine.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SP_BACKUP_ROOT="/mnt/backups/slightly-parallel"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Example entries. A new data root is seeded once with one example
# vision, rule, problem and skill, so the pages are not empty on
# first launch. Set to 0 to start clean.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SP_EXAMPLES=0

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the MCP translator and the Vite dev proxy reach this API.
# Default (unset): http://127.0.0.1:8123. Setup writes the value it
# resolves into each project's generated MCP config.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SP_API="http://127.0.0.1:8123"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Point the Playwright e2e suite at a server that is already up,
# instead of letting it boot its own on :8129.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SP_E2E_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8123"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every name starts with SP_. The three that carried the
# product's former name — SCAN_DATA_ROOT, SCAN_PORT and
# SCAN_CORS_ORIGINS — are still read, after the new ones, so an .env
# written before the rename keeps running. Nothing needs changing.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
